WEBVTT

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:09.310
The Shrine of the Threshold...

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:49.530
Our staggering unemployment is a
consequence of illegal immigrants,

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:51.870
What? This stuff again?
Our staggering unemployment is a
consequence of illegal immigrants,

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:52.530
Our staggering unemployment is a
consequence of illegal immigrants,

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:55.240
who continue to invade our nation
in ever increasing numbers!

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:58.610
Our government is transfixed with
gratifying foreign nations

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:02.310
and makes no real attempt
to resolve this issue.

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:04.410
Our salvation from this issue and
many other issues depends

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:08.410
upon the spiritual independence of
the Japanese people reviving!

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.350
I'm sorry I'm late.

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:15.050
I was held up in traffic.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:19.020
That's all right. We just
arrived ourselves.

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:21.820
Let me introduce you.

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:25.270
Major Shibasaki is the Director of
Aircraft Research and Development

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:26.670
attached to the Research Bureau,

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:30.160
and Captain Okawa is Counselor of
Education in the Training Corps.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:31.910
I'm Shibasaki.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:33.980
I'm Okawa.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.140
I'm Gowa.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:43.280
From a purely tactical standpoint,

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:47.360
rising up and securing temporary
control over this nation militarily

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.150
is not very difficult.

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:52.160
The real issue is what comes next.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:55.320
Capturing the hearts and
minds of the people.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:58.130
There is no denying that it will
be difficult to convince

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:02.300
today's Japanese of the virtue of restoring
our traditions and ideals

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:07.070
revolving around nature, our land, and
our history, instead of money.

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:14.080
But that is all the more reason why
we must be true to our ideals.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:25.150
On the lawn inside the Ichigaya Garrison,

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:30.270
there's a tall old pine tree called
the Shrine of the Threshold

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:34.960
that's stood since the main estate
of the Kishuu Domain existed.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.170
The Shrine of the Threshold?

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.970
Yes, the Shrine of the Threshold.

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:44.310
I don't know the background behind
the name, but perhaps you do?

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:45.800
No, I don't.

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:58.160
But the pine tree's trunk grew hollow
and weak as time passed

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:01.130
and finally, strong winds
brought it down.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.570
The men of the garrison mourned
the loss of the tree,

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:08.340
a tree that had come to
represent the base,

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:10.200
and planted another pine tree
at the exact same location.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.910
After that, the pine tree rooted
itself firmly to the spot,

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:17.970
and grew until it surpassed the beauty
and size of the original.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:23.950
The trunk that grew to be
hollow and weak?

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:27.190
You're implying that the weakened
trunk represents Japan today,

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:30.210
a nation wavering in the strong wind,
ever closer to collapsing.

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:35.160
The newly planted tree rooted
itself firmly to that spot.

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:41.500
Hirokawa, this is how I see it.

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:47.540
The tree grew as part of the land and
environment surrounding itself.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:58.450
Life forms that reject their land and
environment are doomed.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:04.150
People must return to the land from
whence they came. Is that it?

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:09.100
But I highly doubt that neighboring
nations could accept

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.430
such xenophobic intolerance
on our part.

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:15.660
Today one can't expect the rest to adhere
to the values of one nation.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:20.480
Just as the EU once attempted to
shut itself off from the world...

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:23.140
There is no need to shut ourselves
off from the world.

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:27.680
We can leave our ports and gates open.

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:29.680
But we remove the sweet honey that
compels them to come here.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:33.250
We remove the illusion permeated
with poison.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:38.690
What did people gain from
the late 20th century

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:41.800
where everything was driven by greed?

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:44.660
Look at the Japanese people today.

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:48.370
They dwell in a world of
immense wealth,

00:06:48.370 --> 00:06:51.630
but they have lost the ability to be
alert to looming dangers.

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:56.580
Many people are certainly aware
that this dream for prosperity,

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:59.440
the dream that draws the greedy
stream of immigrants here,

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:02.650
is nothing more than an illusion,

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:06.810
but no one attempts to make this
issue their own and resolve it.

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:17.360
But can anyone be expected to be able
to shackle their own desires?

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:21.500
I agree.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:25.400
History has not always been
driven by greed alone.

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:27.440
There is terror also.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:32.550
Motivation is provided by greed, and
terror drives men to action.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:35.410
Are these not the forces behind the
progress of human history?

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:40.620
Terror, jealousy, suspicion...

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:45.460
There is no question that much of human
history has been dominated

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:47.660
by such negative emotions.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:51.900
Long ago, there was a group called the
Kugutsu who held wide influence

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:54.160
over the creation and consolidation
of the Japanese nation.

00:07:56.770 --> 00:08:00.010
It's the legend of a warrior clan
who remained hidden

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:02.240
within the shadows of history like
undercurrents in the oceans.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:08.940
The legend tells the story of
the terror of the Gasaraki.

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:13.790
The ones that are summoned during
the ceremony of Gasaraki,

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:17.660
and remained behind, were powerful
deities called kugai.

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:23.600
The Gasaraki takes the
life of the kugutsu

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.000
in exchange for the power
it leaves behind.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:31.100
But the kugai left behind does not
take the life of the kugutsu.

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:37.040
In fact, they granted an awesome
power for the kugutsu to use.

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:42.380
Eventually the kugai were brought
to the battlefield.

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:50.320
A new terror took hold.
Taboos were broken.

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:53.590
The battlefields were dominated
by unbridled massacres.

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:54.900
All this slowly became
buried in history,

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:58.700
only to be known as legend
with the passage of time.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:00.570
Kugutsu...

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:04.510
Those who tried to rule the land as
puppeteers rule over their puppets

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.200
were known by another name.

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:08.970
The other name was kai.

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:15.080
It is said the kai killed each other
off in an orgy of slaughter.

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:17.720
But others proclaim that the
kai found salvation

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:20.810
by casting aside their powers,
and survive to this day.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:24.550
I don't know which story is true,

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:28.060
but I would like to believe that
the latter tells the truth.

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:33.170
That even today, the Kugutsu Clan
protects the sanctity of the kai.

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:35.400
Could such a thing be possible?

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:41.500
Mr. Gowa, are you aware of the
etymology for the word kugai?

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:43.540
Etymology?

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:46.950
Kugai is written with Chinese characters
for bone and kai or disorder.

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:51.940
Devoid of a soul, the kugai is nothing
more than an empty vessel.

00:09:52.890 --> 00:09:55.620
The kugai can only become
a powerful deity

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:58.320
by taking within itself a kai.

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:02.290
The terror?

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:18.470
If it's a fate that you can't escape,

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:22.610
if it's a fate you can't change,
then you can only accept it.

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:27.820
But that's not true.

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:30.420
Time is not unchanging.

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:33.290
Fate is not carved in stone.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:36.590
These are words that you spoke to me.

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:40.000
That was...

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:42.930
So that was a kugai.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:49.130
I thought you knew about them.

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:51.180
Knew about them?

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:55.950
I suppose I did know about them.

00:10:56.950 --> 00:10:59.580
But how could that be so?

00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:12.700
Who are we?

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:17.300
Are TA pilots simple tools?

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:22.570
Your people refer to the Fakes
as TA's, don't they?

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:24.640
Fakes?

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:28.220
Symbol considers those weapons

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:30.240
a step toward the goal of
reaching Nada.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:34.280
An intermediate step,
and that's why...

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:36.220
Nada?

00:11:36.220 --> 00:11:39.560
Those at Symbol say the word means
"absolute nothingness."

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:44.600
Symbol's goal was not the
development of the Fake.

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:48.160
They wanted to use the Fakes
to summon the Nada.

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:52.340
It's the Gasaraki.

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:55.610
Gasaraki?

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:59.080
No, I can't say anything more.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:04.580
Intelligence loop?

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:08.920
The idea is to incorporate a person
into the AI's architecture

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:12.550
as a sort of external module.

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:16.260
If right, this theory implies that it would
be possible to build an AI

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:21.170
integrated with four billion years
worth of biochemical memory.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:23.200
That this dream could be a reality!

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:26.510
Such possibilities were fascinating
to entertain within our minds,

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:30.310
but no one believed that it could
ever really be achieved.

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:35.080
Then a phenomenon took place before
me that proved this was a reality.

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:37.250
The Mile One?

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:40.520
The relationship between
Mile One and Yushiro

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:43.490
is just like that of an intelligence loop.

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:48.700
So, you wanted to test to see if
something similar would take place

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:50.160
when others are involved?

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:53.760
The person who originally proposed
this theory was...

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:03.440
A researcher who worked at a laboratory
affiliated with Symbol.

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:07.880
Symbol?

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.190
Producing correlation chart.

00:13:15.490 --> 00:13:18.230
What is this? It's all over the map.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:20.730
It's hard to figure out a
pattern, isn't it?

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:24.100
But if you match this up with the
projected operations curve...

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:30.040
So, the two variables peak at
points of negative Tau?

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:33.370
But no correlation could be found with
the Belgistan Lily-painted TA

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:37.040
even after making adjustments
to the Tau variable.

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:41.180
Don't look to me for answers.

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:45.350
In other words, while a strong
correlation exists

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:48.720
between Sat 4's pilot and Captain Gowa,

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:52.520
the correlation was much weaker
against the Belgistan TA.

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:55.730
So something from Yushiro
was being projected to

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:57.530
and reflected back from that pilot?

00:13:57.530 --> 00:14:00.500
That's seems to be the
most likely answer.

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:04.310
The data from this experiment
was sent straight to Gowa

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:07.640
without going through the MOD
research facilities first.

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:11.610
With Colonel Hirokawa and others,
Gowa seems to be moving ahead

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:13.580
with a project that's independent
of the official project.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:19.480
A project that requires quick
results in a hurry.

00:14:20.350 --> 00:14:22.320
Colonel Hirokawa and others?

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:28.720
Father, it's Misuzu. May I come in?

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:30.800
Come in, child.

00:14:34.070 --> 00:14:37.910
What's wrong? Aren't you supposed
to be at school?

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:40.070
Well...

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:42.800
It's Kazukiyo, isn't it?

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:47.180
He's forbidden you from leaving
the house as punishment

00:14:47.180 --> 00:14:49.380
for visiting Kinashi without permission.

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:53.650
Father, what has happened?

00:14:53.650 --> 00:14:56.780
You have not been told yet, have you?

00:14:57.890 --> 00:15:01.230
I am no longer the master of the house.

00:15:05.600 --> 00:15:10.260
I had you come as I had some questions
I need you to answer.

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:13.440
Questions for an old man
such as myself?

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:16.040
First, I want to ask about Yushiro.

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:18.740
Has something happened to Yushiro?

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:23.550
I understand how you would
want to cover for Yushiro.

00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:29.550
But I know that it was you
who aided Yushiro,

00:15:30.190 --> 00:15:33.790
and helped him escape the last
time he visited Kinashi.

00:15:38.070 --> 00:15:39.530
No comment?

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:42.730
No matter.

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:44.910
One more question.

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:47.430
Are you familiar with a man by
the name of Nishida?

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:51.100
If you are referring to Mr. Nishida
of the Gashiin, I know of him.

00:15:52.150 --> 00:15:54.740
I met Mr. Nishida the other day.

00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:57.780
He's an amazing individual.

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:02.620
He made me listen to the legends of
the Kugutsu, me of all people.

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:06.820
Who and what is he?!

00:16:09.430 --> 00:16:13.230
Yes, I am nothing more than
a powerless old man,

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:17.670
sitting aimlessly, watching time flow.

00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:20.140
But why should that be so, Father?!

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:23.070
Because that is the fate of the Gowa.

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:27.400
The one with the most power leads
this family as its master.

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:32.080
The Gowa family has been run like this
from generation to generation.

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:35.180
I myself came into power that way.

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:41.390
The Buddhists say that like a house
set ablaze by flames of desire,

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:45.370
suffering permeates all of life.

00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:48.060
But I believe it's an inferno
that burns one's self.

00:16:50.240 --> 00:16:51.700
Karma?

00:16:56.240 --> 00:17:03.510
Mr. Nishida might have researched
our history thoroughly.

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:08.150
Then could he know about the ceremony
of the Gasaraki as well?

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:13.690
It could be that he has knowledge
of the legends

00:17:13.690 --> 00:17:16.130
that have been lost to the Gowa.

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:19.330
But even if that is the case,

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:23.060
it would be difficult to use that knowledge
to the Gowa's benefit.

00:17:24.070 --> 00:17:25.540
Difficult?

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:30.910
Mr. Kazukiyo, is Mr. Nishida not unlike
a very sharp, old katana?

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:37.250
A sword that has been sharpened
to perfection is too pure.

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:41.290
So pure and dedicated that, in fact,
it will not be possible

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:43.550
to accommodate him with any
manner of deception or bait.

00:17:57.970 --> 00:17:59.700
Why do you pilot a TA?

00:18:00.770 --> 00:18:02.610
Your Fake?

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:04.010
For me...

00:18:04.010 --> 00:18:10.440
No, I pilot the Fake because I can hear
numerous voices talking to me.

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:14.480
My encounter came among
the numerous voices.

00:18:15.020 --> 00:18:16.490
Encounter?

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:20.120
You asked me once,

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:22.890
where am I going to?

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:54.960
Master Sorachi, when did you arrive?

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:58.930
Just a while ago. Mr. Kazukiyo
invited me to come.

00:18:58.930 --> 00:19:00.470
I see.

00:19:00.470 --> 00:19:02.260
Has something happened?

00:19:04.170 --> 00:19:08.730
There was something I wanted
to ask my father.

00:19:09.510 --> 00:19:11.030
Of Mr. Daizaburo?

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:14.280
I'm so afraid.

00:19:14.280 --> 00:19:18.010
Afraid for my big brother, Yushiro.
Anxious about where he's gone to!

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:22.960
Mr. Kazukiyo asked me that same
question just recently as well.

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:27.160
I could not give him an answer.

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:30.320
I only learned of his disappearance
today myself.

00:19:31.430 --> 00:19:32.900
I see.

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:37.400
But I have some notions regarding
where he has gone.

00:19:37.740 --> 00:19:39.370
Where's that?

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:41.070
Probably to Kyoto,

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:44.540
using the path of the kai.

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:46.550
The path of the kai?

00:19:47.380 --> 00:19:51.150
It's a secret network of paths used by
the members of the Kugutsu Clan

00:19:51.150 --> 00:19:55.210
when we needed to travel about
Japan while avoiding detection.

00:19:57.060 --> 00:19:59.790
Few use these paths anymore,

00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:04.390
and now only my branch of the Kugutsu
remain aware of them.

00:20:06.130 --> 00:20:10.070
Are there not other questions
you wish to ask?

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:17.710
Miss Misuzu, how old are you now?

00:20:18.450 --> 00:20:20.250
Fourteen.

00:20:20.250 --> 00:20:21.710
Fourteen years old?

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:26.750
Then I believe you are old enough
to learn the truth.

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:31.890
You want to know the secret behind
Master Yushiro's birth.

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:33.720
Isn't that so?

00:20:36.360 --> 00:20:40.490
I can't remember exactly anymore.

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:45.170
But it seems that the Yushiro I remember
when I was very young

00:20:45.740 --> 00:20:48.540
was different from the Yushiro of today.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:51.910
Then, is he really...

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:55.320
The fourth son of the Daizaburo,
Yushiro Gowa,

00:20:55.320 --> 00:20:59.150
died in an accident eight years ago.

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:00.720
Eight years ago?!

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:02.190
Yes.

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:06.350
Miss Misuzu, did you not travel
to Kinashi recently?

00:21:07.230 --> 00:21:10.590
One of those resting there was the
Yushiro of eight years ago,

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:15.600
or, in others words, the real
Master Yushiro.

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:16.900
Then who is my big brother now?

00:21:16.900 --> 00:21:18.070
A replacement.

00:21:18.070 --> 00:21:21.770
Why? Why would they do such a thing?

00:21:22.310 --> 00:21:24.870
All for the sake of realizing the
ambitions of the Gowa Clan.

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:28.850
That is why they stole the
memories of one boy,

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:31.580
and replaced them with the memories
of the dead boy.

00:21:32.550 --> 00:21:34.020
Ambition?

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:37.460
To summon the terror that we,
the Kugutsu,

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:40.620
left behind over a millennium ago.

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:45.000
To garner the power of the
Gasaraki once again.

00:21:47.900 --> 00:21:49.800
The Ghost of Elsinore...

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:58.170
I pray to be a water logged corpse,
to rest at the spring's bottom.

00:21:59.510 --> 00:22:02.710
'Tis the fate I'd choose if I might be
allowed to be true to the truth.

00:22:24.100 --> 00:22:25.570
This is it.

00:22:30.340 --> 00:22:35.160
Hark

00:22:36.320 --> 00:22:41.610
It's time I journey

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:52.280
Break apart my heart

00:22:52.450 --> 00:22:58.810
For crimson sadness

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:06.320
Pours out from it

00:23:06.530 --> 00:23:10.240
I can only, oh

00:23:10.350 --> 00:23:13.430
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:13.520 --> 00:23:19.040
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:38.140
I can only, oh

00:23:38.230 --> 00:23:41.290
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:41.360 --> 00:23:46.490
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:48.020 --> 00:23:54.470
I beg you, be by my side

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:04.640
Just as flowers and storms are
transient in this world,

00:24:04.640 --> 00:24:06.770
so too is the existence of
people in this world.

00:24:07.370 --> 00:24:09.080
In this realm of existence,

00:24:09.080 --> 00:24:12.810
testaments that signify a mortal's life
are entombed with one's death,

00:24:12.810 --> 00:24:16.410
to make room for new born
life to rejoice anew.

00:24:17.180 --> 00:24:18.850
A kai and a kai

00:24:18.850 --> 00:24:21.490
Enter into the threshold to witness again

00:24:21.490 --> 00:24:24.620
The heartache of youth, the pathos
at the heart of our souls

00:24:25.330 --> 00:24:29.090
As kai we are even denied the purging
of our memory in oblivion.
